```

The outcome is **only** 0 or 1. Any model of this plot has to respect that.

## Cohabiting vs. staying together

```{r}
#| label: bar-cohabit
#| fig-height: 4.4
#| echo: false

couples |>
  count(cohabiting, status) |>
  group_by(cohabiting) |>
  mutate(p = n / sum(n)) |>
  ggplot(aes(cohabiting, p, fill = status)) +
  geom_col(position = "dodge", width = 0.7) +
  scale_fill_manual(values = c(Dissolved = warm_grey, Together = western_purple)) +
  scale_y_continuous(labels = percent_format()) +
