# Appendix {.invert}

## How the data were generated

```{r}
#| eval: false
set.seed(9041)
n <- 320
satisfaction <- round(pmin(pmax(rnorm(n, 4.7, 1.15), 1), 7), 2)
avoidance    <- round(pmin(pmax(rnorm(n, 3.1, 1.10), 1), 7), 2)
cohabiting   <- sample(c("No", "Yes"), n, TRUE, c(0.52, 0.48))

eta <- -0.35 +
  0.85 * (satisfaction - 4.5) -
  0.55 * (avoidance - 3) +
  0.70 * (cohabiting == "Yes")

stayed <- rbinom(n, 1, plogis(eta))
```

Signs in the fitted model should recover this data-generating process: satisfaction +, avoidance −, cohabiting +.
